    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d780">

                <pb facs="0868" n="674" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg674"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Austria)/7–2345:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 780<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Political Adviser for Austrian
                        Affairs</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Erhardt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Acting Secretary of State</hi><anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d780-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Verona</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-23T14:00:00+02:00">July 23, 1945—2 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>126. July 21 Koniev sent letter to United
                    States, British, and French commanders stating he had been instructed facilitate
                    occupation of various sectors Vienna by our forces. Gruenther, Winterton
                    <pb facs="0869" n="675" xml:id="pg675"/> and Cherrière invited to Vienna meeting 1 p.m., July 24, to settle
                    problems discussed at July 16 conference re taking over and they have accepted.
                    US reconnaissance party moving to Vienna July 22 and July 24.</p>
                <p>Soviet began evacuating Styria July 22 but were not quite ready to move into
                    Upper Austria north of Danube. Soviet Genl who went to Linz for preliminary
                    arrangements was reported as most cooperative.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Erhardt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d780-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d780-f1-content">
                <p>The gist of this message was included in telegram No. 126 of July 25 from
                        Grew to Byrnes (file No. 800.00 Summaries/7–2545).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
